        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tanghe River Park\n- Products: Red Ribbon\n- Organizations: American Society of Landscape Architects, Condé Nast Traveler, National Magazine Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Tanghe River Park was created on the coast of the Tanghe River in July 2006.\n- The Red Ribbon is a red steel bench that stretches for half a kilometre through Tanghe River Park.\n- The Red Ribbon at Tanghe River Park won an honor award from the American Society of Landscape Architects.\n- Readers of Condé Nast Traveler chose the Red Ribbon as one of the seven wonders of the architectural world.\n- Condé Nast Traveler has won twenty-five National Magazine Awards.",
